WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.287
Here's the federal side of the first gate.

2
00:00:02.287 --> 00:00:06.915
Account management treats non-person
identities as a defined account type,

3
00:00:06.915 --> 00:00:08.825
each with an owner and a sponsor.

4
00:00:08.825 --> 00:00:14.263
The evidence is this gate's record, plus
the kit runs for owners and agent sponsors.

5
00:00:14.263 --> 00:00:18.583
Identifier management means each
identity has its own identifier,

6
00:00:18.583 --> 00:00:20.975
joined to its record and never reused.

7
00:00:20.975 --> 00:00:23.600
To validate, four read-only checks run.

8
00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:28.901
One lists Active Directory accounts whose
passwords never expire or are too old,

9
00:00:28.901 --> 00:00:31.750
each joined to a record
or listed as unowned.

10
00:00:31.750 --> 00:00:37.075
One reports zero apps with no owner, and
a dated finding for any with just one.

11
00:00:37.075 --> 00:00:40.988
One lists every managed identity
and its role assignments.

12
00:00:40.988 --> 00:00:46.000
And one lists agent identities with their
sponsors, where the tenant exposes them.

13
00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:49.737
The inventory's Graph reads are
listed for the government clouds.

14
00:00:49.737 --> 00:00:53.767
Agent identities are generally
available in commercial,

15
00:00:53.767 --> 00:00:55.950
and in GCC with documented gaps.

16
00:00:55.950 --> 00:01:00.100
And there's nothing to roll back,
because the inventory only reads.
